        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.645,
            0.064,
            0.834,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "The Other Side of Zero"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.121,
            0.558,
            0.142
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Addition to keep track of movement"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.15,
            0.833,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": "Start from the Food Court and press + 2 in the lift. Where will you reach?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.202,
            0.592,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": "We can describe this using an expression:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.231,
            0.617,
            0.252
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Starting Floor + Movement = Target Floor."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.26,
            0.834,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": "The starting floor is + 1 (Food Court) and the number of button presses is + 2. Therefore, you reach the target floor **(+ 1) + (+ 2) = + 3** (Book Store)."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.337,
            0.302,
            0.359
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.367,
            0.833,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": "1. You start from Floor + 2 and press – 3 in the lift. Where will you reach? Write an expression for this movement."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.416,
            0.834,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": "2. Evaluate these expressions (you may think of them as Starting Floor + Movement by referring to the Building of Fun)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.46,
            0.416,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "a. (+ 1) + (+ 4) ="
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.533,
            0.46,
            0.755,
            0.48
          ],
          "content": "b. (+ 4) + (+ 1) ="
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.482,
            0.417,
            0.501
          ],
          "content": "c. (+ 4) + (–   3) ="
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.534,
            0.482,
            0.755,
            0.501
          ],
          "content": "d. (– 1) + (+ 2) ="
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.503,
            0.416,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "e. (– 1) + (+ 1) ="
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.534,
            0.503,
            0.772,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "f. 0 + (+ 2) ="
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.525,
            0.426,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": "g. 0 + (–2) = \\_"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.552,
            0.833,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": "3. Starting from different floors, find the movements required to reach Floor – 5. For example, if I start at Floor + 2, I must press – 7 to reach Floor – 5. The expression is (+ 2) + (– 7) = – 5."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.55,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.617,
            0.833,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": "Find more such starting positions and the movements needed to reach Floor –5 and write the expressions."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.673,
            0.626,
            0.695
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Combining button presses is also addition"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.699,
            0.834,
            0.79
          ],
          "content": "Gurmit was in the Toy Store and wanted to go down two floors. But by mistake he pressed the ‘+’ button two times. He realised his mistake and quickly pressed the ‘–’ button three times. How many floors below or above the Toy Store will Gurmit reach?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.797,
            0.834,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "Gurmit will go one floor down. We can show the movement resulting from combining button presses as an expression: $(+2)+(-3)=-1$"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.883,
            0.941,
            0.917,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": "245"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
